  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In the same plane, \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) are three distinct lines. If \\(a\\perp b\\) and \\(b\\perp c\\), what is the positional relationship between \\(a\\) and \\(c\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a\\perp c\\)",
    "B": "\\(a\\) and \\(c\\) intersect but are not perpendicular.",
    "C": "\\(a\\parallel c\\)",
    "D": "\\(a\\) and \\(c\\) coincide."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Both \\(a\\) and \\(c\\) are perpendicular to \\(b\\). In the same plane, two lines perpendicular to the same line are parallel to each other, so \\(a\\parallel c\\).",
